  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Tangella Sambasiva Rao vs The State Of Ap on 12 September, 2019 Author: U. Durga Prasad Rao Bench: U. Durga Prasad Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice U. Durga Prasad Rao Criminal Petition No.4958 Of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "The petitioners/A1 to A3 seek to quash the proceedings against them in Crime No.208 of 2017 of Addanki Police Station, Prakasam District, which was registered against them for the offences under Sections 273, 188 of IPC and Secs.58, 59 and 63 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (for short 'FSS Act, 2006). 2. The allegations against the petitioners briefly are that on 16.11.2017 at 9:00 P.M., the Station House Officer along with staff, on credible information proceeded to the house of A1 situated at Post Office centre, Addanki Village, seized the banned tobacco products under a cover of panchanama, later he arrested them and registered a case in Crime No.208 of 2017 for the offences stated supra. 3.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for petitioners while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for petitioners while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
